    "verdict_tag": "PRUNE",
    "verdict": "PRUNE (scope-(a)). Cross-check: B_AME/B_base reproduces mu_ext_target for all four isotopes (True). mu_ext is NON-MONOTONE (order 4He/T/D/3He, spread ×59.12, deuteron 2nd-largest from its tiny B_base). NO parameter-free per-knot reading of the additive S(K)/tr_M structure reproduces that shape: every candidate that has 4He as the max (S/m_e, S/(A m_e), 1/tr_M, constit_sum/tr_M) puts the DEUTERON SMALLEST (rank 4), the exact opposite of mu_ext's D-at-rank-2 — the per-knot S/(A m_e) family is monotone/compressed (spread ×1.14 across the four) and cannot supply mu_ext's ×2.83 non-monotone range, as the formalize-first uniformity argument predicts. tr_M(K) itself is anti-shaped (4He MIN, not max). JUNK CONTROL: the best real candidate (S/(A*m_e), Spearman +0.80) does NOT beat the best junk control (JUNK:A, Spearman +0.63) by a meaningful n=4 margin (beats_by_>0.25=False) — so any apparent partial match is within look-elsewhere noise. CONCLUSION: the per-knot additive S(K) structure does NOT inform the derived k(A) extensivity multiplier; it is pruned as a source of the non-monotone k(A). Scope-limited negative (a): constrains the per-knot S(K)/tr_M single-quantity reading only; NOT a structural exclusion of tr_M in a richer multi-term / operator-valued branching combiner (GAP-A-3/GAP-A-4 remain the open derived directions). No fit, no BW, no rescaler-as-closure.",
